{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>האמור</b> — The way of instruction is to say to a king of worthlessness, and to say: wicked one, to one of the nobles. And all the more so He who does not show partiality to princes and does not recognize, like יכיר."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Reading ולא נכר as 'and does not recognize'; the text may be elliptical or corrupt. The word יכיר appears in Hebrew script without gloss; left untranslated as the argument appears to turn on the form itself."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:28.760468543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}